Qwaszx86 wrote:
>
> Do you head for Sokoban before the mines, or mines first?

That is a question of personal tastes and playing styles.

Before I learned to run away up the stairs at the first sign of
trouble, I was more likely to survive doing Sokoban first.
After I learned it, the rapid level gains in the mines allowed
me to survive Sokoban better.

Sometimes I do a level of each.  Fully explore the level of
the regular dungeon below the mines, fully explore one level
of the mines.  Fully explore the second level of the regular
dungeon, fully explore next level of the mines.  Then when
I find Sokoban move up in it at a similar pace.

Sometimes I explore to mine town, then do Sokoban, then
go deeper into the mines.

Both compromises work for me a little better than doing
either first.

Then one day I played a game where a portal to Ludios
appeared before the stairs up to Sokoban so I explored
Ludios first.  Sigh.  Bad mistake without reflection.

> I find I often end up burdened (or just dead) if
